00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:07.839 align:start position:0%
European Union ministers will discuss  new rules aimed at better protecting  workers who are temporarily posted  abroad by their employers that talks in  Luxembourg on October 15 the EU is  striving to guarantee the rights and  working conditions off posted workers  throughout the Union it also aims to  halt social dumping where foreign  service providers undercut local  concerns with lower labor standards the  so-called posting of workers directive  is aimed at ensuring certain minimum  terms and conditions of employment on  things like working hours conditions pay  equal opportunity and annual leave but  it also obliges member states to grab  public access to information about  national employment conditions the  minister's aim to agree on a general  approach to strengthening those rules  the council will also exchange views on  youth unemployment with around one and  four people under 25 out of work on  average last year across the EU  according to the eurostat statistics  agency The ministers will take stock of  progress made with current initiatives  to find jobs for young Europeans in Lyon  with recommendations by EU leaders in  June the ministers who are responsible  for employment the protection of health  social and consumer interests gender  equality and equal opportunities will  also study this year's European semester  process the six-month monitoring and  support mechanism is aimed at helping  member states to better plan their  budgets and economic policies in  Luxembourg the council will look at the  employment and social aspects of the  mechanism to prepare for 2014
 

